  //
  //  After every restart: set 8931, 8932, 8933 and 8934 to PUBLIC in
  //  the Ports panel. That visibility does not persist.
  //
  //  2026-08-18: supergateway is now PINNED LOCALLY at
  //  Startup\node_modules\supergateway (v3.4.3) and launched with
  //  node directly. It used to run as "npx -y supergateway", which
  //  hit the npm registry three times on every folder open - slow,
  //  and it fails outright when the network is flaky.
  //  Backup of the previous file: tasks.json.pre-local-supergateway-backup
  //  A watchdog scheduled task (CoworkBridgeWatchdog) probes the
  //  ports every 2 minutes and restarts any that have died.
  //  2026-09-02: the watchdog covers ALL FOUR ports including 8934,
  //  with per-port flags matching this file. Verified live via
  //  watchdog\status.txt. Trust _bridge-watchdog.ps1, not this note.
  //
  //  2026-08-21: 8932 and 8933 now run STATELESS. --stateful and
  //  --sessionTimeout 1800000 were removed from those two tasks: the
  //  30-minute idle expiry silently dropped all three tool surfaces
  //  mid-session on 2026-08-20 while every process stayed alive.
  //  Stateful also measured a 16% call-drop rate on 8932 and did not
  //  fix the 8933 long-job kill. 8931 KEEPS --stateful - it is required
  //  for the Playwright Edge SSO profile lock - and must never get
  //  --isolated, which would lose SSO.
  //  Backup of the previous file: tasks.json.pre-stateless-8932-8933-backup
  //
  //  2026-08-21: the "Cowork Autorun Watcher (no port)" task was REMOVED.
  //  AUTORUN.ps1 is not an approved execution path for Cowork - if 8933 is
  //  unreachable the rule is to STOP and report, never to route work to
  //  COPILOT_COWORK\autorun\queue. Auto-starting the watcher left that
  //  path armed and inviting. The script itself is untouched on disk and
  //  can still be run by hand; only the folderOpen auto-start is gone.
  //
  //  2026-09-02: ADDED the Power Automate Bridge on 8934. It follows the
  //  8932/8933 STATELESS pattern deliberately - no --stateful, no
  //  --sessionTimeout - per the 2026-08-21 finding above.
  //  It exists because the Power Platform CLI cannot reach flows: there is
  //  no `pac flow` command group, `pac admin` has no flow subcommand, and
  //  `pac auth token` mints only the api.powerplatform.com audience, which
  //  returned 401 against both the Dataverse workflow table and
  //  api.flow.microsoft.com. Measured 2026-09-02; evidence in
  //  Outputs\2026-09-02 - Flow CRUD Interface Probe.
  //  The server is INERT by design until an Entra app registration is wired
  //  into FlowBridge\flow-bridge.config.json: auth_strategy is "none",
  //  read_only is true, allow_delete is false and no environment is
  //  allowlisted, so every flow tool refuses with a clear reason.
  //  Backup of the previous file: tasks.json.pre-8934-backup
  // ==========================================================
